From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude Opus 5.5" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 18:37:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 23/25] IbashoAgent readNotecard and findRegion

A notecard given to an agent could only be read through a script in one
of its own objects, so not on land where it can't build; and a teleport
to a region name that doesn't exist just never happened.

readNotecard {item_id, timeout=20} -> {item_id, name, text, items:
[{name, type}], truncated?} reads a notecard in the agent's inventory as
the notecard preview does: only with copy permission, the asset through
the asset storage, the Linden text parsed as the text editor imports it
(versions 0 to 2). Items embedded in the text show as [type: name]; the
text is at most 64 KB, and an asset over 1 MB is refused.

findRegion {name, timeout=10} -> {found, region: {name, global, access,
maturity}} or {found: false, similar} looks a region up as the world
map's search does (MapNameRequest). A hook in
LLWorldMapMessage::processMapBlockReply hands each map block over; the
empty block that ends a name search says the map has answered, so "no
such region" is told apart from no answer.
